From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: checksum only shared and scanout render targets

Transaction elimination (a CRC per 16x16 tile, an unchanged tile is not
written back) pays off on buffers whose content stays partly the same
from frame to frame: window and scanout buffers (UI, bezels, black
bands). Emulators render into off-screen targets they redraw completely
every frame, where the CRC never skips a tile and only adds the CRC
computation and the CRC buffer traffic. Measured on a Mali-G31 MP1
(H700), PPSSPP God of War: fragment engine 64-65 % busy with CRC on every
render target, 50-57 % with PAN_MESA_DEBUG=nocrc; a 2D game (SNES) the
same either way. Keep the CRC for render targets that are shared or
scanned out.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -536,8 +536,12 @@
    unsigned bytes_per_pixel = MAX2(pres->base.nr_samples, 1) *
                               util_format_get_blocksize(pres->base.format);
 
+   /* Off-screen targets are usually redrawn whole every frame: the CRC
+    * only costs there. Window and scanout buffers keep it. */
+   bool presented = pres->base.bind & (PIPE_BIND_SHARED | PIPE_BIND_SCANOUT);
+
    return pres->base.bind & PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET && panfrost_is_2d(pres) &&
-          bytes_per_pixel <= bytes_per_pixel_max &&
+          presented && bytes_per_pixel <= bytes_per_pixel_max &&
           pres->base.last_level == 0 && !(dev->debug & PAN_DBG_NO_CRC);
 }
 
